CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*vdev->irq)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_platform_irq)...)
#167: FILE: drivers/vfio/platform/vfio_platform_irq.c:41:
+	vdev->irq = kzalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_platform_irq) * cnt, GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

